		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: TYT MD-UV380 DMR Rx Missing]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2926&amp;p=31200#p31200"><![CDATA[
I see its been a couple of months since the last reply to this thread, but, instead of starting a new one, I thought I should post here first.<br>I just recently purchased a UV390 w/gps. I am using OpenGD77 and have this same "Rx Missing" issue. I am using a Raspberry Pi 3b duplex hotspot at home as there are no repeaters near me. For mobile, I use a  Pi Zero 2w also duplex with a Tmobile wifi hotspot. The problem is the same regardless of which hotspot or wifi connection I am using. <br>For me, it does not occur during a receive but rather, between contacts. Here is an example,, if I am monitoring a qso, when one person finishes and un-keys the mic, when the next person keys up and starts talking, I see the signal being received on the rssi bar, but no audio is coming out of the speaker. If I give the channel knob a quick click one direction or the other and back again, or a quick tap on the ptt, the audio then comes out the speaker. This is random and not a consistent issue. It may happen 2-3 times during a conversation, or not at all. I have tried putting the 868 on the same channel and when the 390 drops the audio, the 868 does not. It is very inconvenient to have to have two radios going because the one is unreliable. It is also inconvenient to have to constantly monitor the rssi bar to see if anyone has started talking and I'm just not hearing it. <br>Some things I have tried: updated to firmware 20240412, no difference. Various filters, dmr, ts, etc on or off,, no change. Eco positions, no change. Dmr crc on or off (not sure what it does) no change. Changed my Tx and Rx freqs to have a wider separation.. no change.<br>I really like the firmware and the cps is much more intuitive to my brain than the anytone is. I hope the information I have given as to how and when it occurs is helpful to the developers. If you need any more info, I would be happy to assist. <br>Thank you and 73<br>Rowe ~ N0BFC<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5955">N0BFC</a> — Wed May 08, 2024 3:46 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
