		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: TYT MD-UV380 DMR Rx Missing]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2926&amp;p=30040#p30040"><![CDATA[
The codec is the same in all the radios, from the single band MD380 onwards. (Note we don't support the MD380 because it uses an older version of DMR chip)<br><br>The reason we were able to use the codec is only becasue Travis Goodspeed found and analysed the codec in the MD380, and we were able to use his analysis to find the location of the codec in the other radios.<br><br>It is too complicated for us to use the codec from each individual radio, because when the location of the codec changes in the official file, it requires changes to both the CPS and the firmware to use the codec in the different location, and as the codec binary is identical this would be a pointless waste of time and effort.<br><br>All firmware for both TYT and Baofeng radios is written by the same external software development organisation, the write the codec and the application firmware and also the bootloader for all the TYT and Baofeng radios, which we support.<br>We believe that this 'organisation' is a state run company, rather than a private enterprise and hence has no company name<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Mar 09, 2024 4:17 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
