Thank you for the reply, highly appreciated. <br>This missing audio occurs quite frequent, once an hour or so, and this is the second transceiver I use, the MDUV390, but the previous one, an RT3S GPS behaved identical. That was the reason to sell it. A while I stayed with an Alinco MD5 (older brother of the new Anytone) but I really missed the features developed by you guys, satellite with doppler, audio leveling, large memory to store all the users to date etc. That''s why I have the MD390 today again <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"> Maybe the MD9600 codec being imported is not the same, or something is happening at the beginning at the reception and not everything initialises properly, who knows... I agree, hardware logging in real time can be a hassle, but I had to change back to the original FW just because people in traffic told me ... "well, we asked you something 30 minutes ago and you disappeared... " <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"> It looked rude i did not responded, but this was a complete miss. Thanks for the reply, looking forward for the news on this topic.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4323">YO2AP</a> — Fri Mar 08, 2024 6:43 pm</p><hr />
